From: jayweihung <3034830+jayweihung@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:59:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] feat: hc relations says who waits for whom among the
 agents running now

A terminal's record keeps its status words of the last day (history,
at most 40). terminal.relations reads every machine's records (or one
machine's, with on) and returns the waits between agents (with the
reminder to type), chains of waits that end stuck or loop, agents
working in one folder, agents waiting for a person, and idle ones
nobody waits for, so every app shows the same judgement.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
